        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "bd79f16a-674d-5b7f-97d0-134a8d8466c8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Augustus Jesse Bowie Jr.\n- Products: Large-capacity electrical switches, 287 kV disconnecting switch\n- Laws: Rural Electrification Act of 1936\n- Organizations: Rural electric cooperative\n- Places: West Coast of the United States, rural United States\n- Topics: Electrification, rural electrification, New Deal\n\nFacts:\n- During the 1910s and 1920s, Augustus Jesse Bowie Jr.'s early innovations in large-capacity electrical switches, including the 287 kV disconnecting switch, helped the spread of electrification on the West Coast of the United States.\n- On May 20, 1936, the Rural Electrification Act of 1936 was enacted to provide federal loans for electrical distribution systems serving isolated rural areas of the United States.\n- In the 1930s, Augustus Jesse Bowie Jr.'s switch innovations became essential to the New Deal's mass-scale rural electrification efforts.\n- A newly formed rural electric cooperative was funded by the Rural Electrification Act of 1936.\n- At that time, the Renwick Generating Plant began supplying power to the newly formed rural electric cooperative.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ecef6a04-63e1-5069-93cf-edf935c16c3d",
        "text": "Page: Augustus Jesse Bowie Jr.. Sentence: His crucial early innovations in large-capacity electrical switches, including the 1000lb.\nPage: Augustus Jesse Bowie Jr.. Sentence: 287Kv disconnecting switch, were important in the early spread of electrification on the West Coast of the United States during the 1910's-1920s, and became essential to the New Deal's mass-scale rural electrification efforts in the 1930s.\nPage: Rural Electrification Act. Sentence: The Rural Electrification Act of 1936, enacted on May 20, 1936, provided federal loans for the installation of electrical distribution systems to serve isolated rural areas of the United States.\nPage: Renwick Generating Plant. Sentence: At that time the plant started to supply power to a newly formed rural electric cooperative that was funded by the Rural Electrification Act of 1936.",
